Q2. REAL-TIME UPDATES & POLLING BOTTLENECKS (KDS & CALL WAITER)
================================================================================
Question:
Currently, Streamlit polls FastAPI for KDS tickets and Call Waiter alerts. If Zaika scales from 6 tables in one restaurant to 500 restaurants with 10,000 concurrent diners, polling will crush your MySQL database. How would you re-architect real-time updates?

Model Answer:
1. Replace HTTP Polling with WebSockets / SSE: For the Kitchen Display System and Staff Floor Map, replace periodic GET polling with FastAPI WebSockets or Server-Sent Events (SSE) backed by Redis Pub/Sub.
2. Event-Driven Push: When a customer places an order or taps "Call Waiter", FastAPI writes to MySQL and publishes an event to a restaurant-specific Redis channel (e.g., restaurant:101:kds). Only connected kitchen and staff tablets for that restaurant receive an instant push update, dropping idle database read queries by over 95%.

