Q3. SECURITY & QR CODE SPOOFING PREVENTION
================================================================================
Question:
Your customer QR menu requires zero login (?table=T1&token=tok_t1_99a1). What stops a prankster from saving that URL at home and placing Rs. 50,000 worth of fake orders for Table T1 three days later?

Model Answer:
1. Rotating Session Tokens: Instead of a permanent static qr_token, implement a dynamic session token that rotates automatically every time a table resets to Empty after payment, or expires after a 2-hour dining window.
2. Two-Step Staff Confirmation Gate: Zaika includes a human-in-the-loop safeguard—customer orders enter as 'Placed' and do not fire to the kitchen until floor staff visually verify the occupied table and click "Send to Kitchen".
3. Rate Limiting & Geofencing: Add Redis-backed rate limiting (e.g., max 3 unconfirmed orders per table per 10 minutes) and optional restaurant WiFi IP/geofence validation.

