Q4. DATABASE DESIGN & HISTORICAL DATA INTEGRITY
================================================================================
Question:
Why did you store unit_price inside order_items when price_full and price_half already exist in menu_items? Doesn't that violate 3NF database normalization?

Model Answer:
1. Intentional Denormalization for Point-in-Time Accuracy: Strictly speaking, storing unit_price in order_items is a deliberate, controlled denormalization—and it is essential in e-commerce and POS systems.
2. Business Justification: If the restaurant owner raises Paneer Tikka from Rs. 260 to Rs. 300 next week, referencing menu_items.price_full dynamically would retroactively corrupt historical bills, tax reports, and GST audits from past months. Storing unit_price preserves an immutable financial snapshot of what the customer actually agreed to pay at order time.

