Q6. DATABASE QUERY OPTIMIZATION & INDEXING (OWNER ANALYTICS)
================================================================================
Question:
Your Owner Dashboard runs SUM and GROUP BY queries across orders and order_items to calculate daily revenue and top-selling dishes. After 2 years and 5 million rows, that dashboard takes 8 seconds to load. How do you bring it under 50 milliseconds?

Model Answer:
1. Composite Indexing: Add composite indexes on (status, placed_at) in orders and (menu_item_id, order_id) in order_items so MySQL performs fast index range scans instead of full table scans.
2. Pre-Aggregated Materialized Summary Tables: Historical days never change. Instead of recalculating 5 million rows on every dashboard load, a nightly cron job or event consumer aggregates closed orders into a daily_sales_summary table. The dashboard then queries 1 row per day plus only today's live orders.
3. Redis Caching: Cache the Owner Dashboard summary response in Redis with a 30-second TTL (Time-To-Live).

