Q7. DISTRIBUTED KDS CONSISTENCY (PARTIAL STATION COMPLETION)
================================================================================
Question:
Suppose Table T2 orders Tandoori Roti (Tandoor station) and Butter Chicken (Curry station). Tandoor finishes in 4 minutes, while Curry takes 16 minutes. How does your data model handle partial readiness without serving cold bread?

Model Answer:
1. Granular Item-Level State Machine: The schema decouples orders.status (macro order state) from order_items.item_status (micro station state: Pending -> Cooking -> Ready).
2. Synchronized Dispatch: Each station marks its own items Ready independently. The KDS UI displays a progress indicator (e.g., "1/2 Items Ready") and only triggers the final "Ready for Pickup" alert to floor staff when COUNT(*) WHERE item_status != 'Ready' reaches 0, ensuring all dishes arrive hot together.

