Q8. FASTAPI PERFORMANCE (ASYNC VS. SYNC BOTTLENECKS)
================================================================================
Question:
FastAPI is famous for async/await high concurrency, yet standard SQLAlchemy sessions (SessionLocal) and pymysql are synchronous blocking calls. How does mixing async def routes with blocking database calls hurt throughput in FastAPI?

Model Answer:
1. Event Loop Blocking: If you declare an endpoint with async def and run a blocking synchronous db.query() inside it, Python blocks the single-threaded Uvicorn event loop, freezing all other incoming requests until MySQL responds.
2. The Fix: Either define endpoints with standard def (so FastAPI automatically runs them safely in an external threadpool) or upgrade the data layer to SQLAlchemy 2.0 AsyncSession with the non-blocking aiomysql / asyncmy driver.

